Prototype Pattern
It allows to create new objects by copying/ cloning an existing object.

This is especially useful when the creation process is complex or resource-intensive.

Without Prototype Pattern :
Creating new objects involves directly instantiating new instances, which can be costly and requires knowledge of the object’s class.

With Prototype Pattern :
New objects are created by copying an existing prototype instance, which can be more efficient and simplifies the creation of complex objects with similar structures.


Example :

Using the clone method, we can simply return a clone Student object. Also we can change attributes using getters and setters.
If there are many attributes and those attributes come from the database, if we crate a new object, it will take time.
Using the prototype pattern we can copy the existing object which is efficient.